---
// Layer 1 of sol-019, for accumulation: the Answer.
//
// RUNG NUMBERING, stated here because getting it wrong cost a round trip on
// 16 Aug: every question the page asks is a rung, and THE ANSWER IS RUNG 1.
// So: 1 Answer, 2 rates, 3 money flow, 4 growth, 5 sequence, 6 protection,
// 7 expert. My own comments had been counting from the rates rung, so a report
// about "rung 3" was answered in rung 4 and the real defect stayed shipped.
//
// Three inputs, opinionated defaults for everything else, and a result stated
// as a sentence. Everything the old page asked for up front - a seed capital
// field, a step-up, an inflation rate, three allocation sliders, four
// allocation presets, a tax toggle and a mode switch between "FORWARD:
// STOCHASTIC" and "REVERSE: GOAL-SEEK" - is still there, one layer down,
// because all of it is an assumption rather than something the visitor arrived
// knowing.
//
// This component is also the page's compute host. One worker, one simulation,
// broadcast to every surface (sol-026, dd-013).
---

<section
  id="sipAnswerLayer"
  class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 pt-6 pb-2"
  aria-label="Your savings plan"
>
  <div class="card-premium rounded-2xl p-6 sm:p-8 space-y-7">

    <p class="text-sm text-navy-500 dark:text-navy-400">
      Three questions. You can change everything else afterwards.
    </p>

    <!-- The three inputs, phrased as a sentence rather than a form -->
    <div class="space-y-4 text-base sm:text-lg leading-relaxed text-navy-800 dark:text-navy-200">
      <div class="flex flex-wrap items-baseline gap-x-3 gap-y-2">
        <label for="sipAnsMonthly" class="shrink-0">I can put away</label>
        <span class="inline-flex items-baseline gap-1 border-b-2 border-gold-500/60 focus-within:border-gold-500 transition-colors">
          <span class="text-navy-500 dark:text-navy-400">₹</span>
          <input
            id="sipAnsMonthly" type="text" inputmode="numeric" value="25,000"
            class="w-28 sm:w-32 bg-transparent py-0.5 font-semibold tabular-nums text-navy-900 dark:text-navy-100 focus:outline-none"
          />
        </span>
        <span class="shrink-0">a month</span>
      </div>

      <div class="flex flex-wrap items-baseline gap-x-3 gap-y-2">
        <label for="sipAnsYears" class="shrink-0">for</label>
        <span class="inline-flex items-baseline border-b-2 border-gold-500/60 focus-within:border-gold-500 transition-colors">
          <input
            id="sipAnsYears" type="text" inputmode="numeric" value="20"
            class="w-14 bg-transparent py-0.5 font-semibold tabular-nums text-navy-900 dark:text-navy-100 focus:outline-none"
          />
        </span>
        <span class="shrink-0">years,</span>
      </div>

      <div class="flex flex-wrap items-baseline gap-x-3 gap-y-2">
        <label for="sipAnsTarget" class="shrink-0">and I want</label>
        <span class="inline-flex items-baseline gap-1 border-b-2 border-gold-500/60 focus-within:border-gold-500 transition-colors">
          <span class="text-navy-500 dark:text-navy-400">₹</span>
          <!-- The default goal is deliberately one this default plan MISSES,
               and misses by a human amount. The figure inherited from the old
               page was 5 crore against 25,000 a month, which the plan misses
               eightfold: every lever then reads as a joke - put away 2.12 lakh
               a month, or wait past your own lifetime - and the reader learns
               nothing except that the tool is not talking to them. A gap of
               about 40 lakh is one all three levers can close in a way a person
               can actually weigh, which is the point of offering them. -->
          <input
            id="sipAnsTarget" type="text" inputmode="numeric" value="1,00,00,000"
            class="w-40 sm:w-44 bg-transparent py-0.5 font-semibold tabular-nums text-navy-900 dark:text-navy-100 focus:outline-none"
          />
        </span>
        <span class="shrink-0">at the end of it.</span>
      </div>

      <!-- dd-004 and dd-017. The frame was stated for the goal and not for the
           contribution, so the page took one input in today's money and the
           other in rupees that quietly decayed for twenty years.
           BOTH are in today's money now, and the interpretation is STATED
           rather than asked: a mode question here would be a fourth input at
           the very step that exists to have only three. -->
      <div class="text-xs leading-relaxed text-navy-500 dark:text-navy-400 pl-0.5 space-y-1.5">
        <p>
          <span class="font-semibold text-navy-600 dark:text-navy-300">Both amounts are in today's money.</span>
          ₹1 crore means what a crore buys now, not what the number will read in
          twenty years. And ₹25,000 a month means ₹25,000 of today's spending
          power — so we raise the instalment each year in line with prices to
          keep it worth that. <span id="sipAnsEscalation" class="text-navy-600 dark:text-navy-300"></span>
        </p>
        <p>
          When you retire you will ask for an income that holds its value, not a
          fixed number of rupees. It is only fair to invest the same way.
          <button type="button" id="sipAnsOpenContribution"
                  class="underline decoration-dotted underline-offset-2 hover:text-navy-700 dark:hover:text-navy-200 cursor-pointer">
            Change how your contribution grows
          </button>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- The answer -->
    <div class="pt-6 border-t border-navy-200 dark:border-navy-800">
      <p id="sipAnsHeadline"
         class="text-lg sm:text-xl leading-snug font-medium text-navy-900 dark:text-navy-100">
        Working it out…
      </p>
      <p id="sipAnsDetail" class="text-sm text-navy-600 dark:text-navy-400 mt-2 leading-relaxed"></p>

      <!-- Assumptions, visible at the point of use, not buried in a tooltip -->
      <p class="text-xs text-navy-500 dark:text-navy-400 mt-4">
        <span id="sipAnsAssumptions">Working out the assumptions…</span>
        <button
          id="sipAnsOpenDetail" type="button"
          class="underline underline-offset-2 decoration-dotted hover:text-gold-600 dark:hover:text-gold-400 focus:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-gold-500/50 rounded"
        >Change these</button>
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- The levers. Hidden when the plan already gets there. -->
    <div id="sipAnsRemedies" class="hidden pt-5 border-t border-navy-200 dark:border-navy-800">
      <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-navy-500 dark:text-navy-400 mb-3">
        To get there, change one of these
      </p>
      <div id="sipAnsRemedyGrid" class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-3 gap-3"></div>
      <p class="text-xs text-navy-500 dark:text-navy-400 mt-3">
        Tap one to apply it.
      </p>
    </div>

  </div>
</section>

<script>
  import { contributionPlan, instalmentInYear } from '../../utils/sipAdvice';
  import {
    readSipInputs,
    syncAdvancedFromEntry,
    syncEntryFromAdvanced,
  } from '../../utils/sipInputs';

  const $ = (id: string) => document.getElementById(id);
  const grp = (n: number) => n.toLocaleString('en-IN', { maximumFractionDigits: 0 });

  // A layperson reads crore and lakh, not 59,500,000.
  function money(n: number): string {
    const v = Math.round(n);
    if (v >= 10000000) return `₹${(v / 10000000).toFixed(2)} crore`;
    if (v >= 100000) return `₹${(v / 100000).toFixed(1)} lakh`;
    return `₹${grp(v)}`;
  }

  let worker: Worker | null = null;

  // Every figure on this screen is in today's prices, stated as such. Rung 3
  // shows both moneys side by side; there is no mode to keep in sync, because a
  // difference that matters cannot be hidden behind a control (dd-006).
  const readInputs = readSipInputs;

  function renderEscalation(inputs: any) {
    const el = $('sipAnsEscalation');
    if (!el) return;
    const plan = contributionPlan(inputs);
    const last = instalmentInYear(inputs, inputs.horizonYears);
    if (!plan.holdsPurchasingPower) {
      el.textContent =
        `You have set a flat ₹${grp(plan.monthly)} a month, so by year ` +
        `${inputs.horizonYears} it will buy about ` +
        `₹${grp(plan.monthly / Math.pow(1 + inputs.expectedInflation / 100, inputs.horizonYears - 1))} ` +
        `of what it buys today.`;
      return;
    }
    el.textContent =
      `That means paying ₹${grp(last)} a month by year ${inputs.horizonYears} — ` +
      `worth the same ₹${grp(plan.monthly)} you can afford now.`;
  }

  function renderAnswer(inputs: any, outlook: any) {
    const headline = $('sipAnsHeadline')!;
    const detail = $('sipAnsDetail')!;
    const years = inputs.horizonYears;
    const odds = Math.round(outlook.odds * 100);
    const frame = inputs.isPostTax
      ? `in today's money, after the tax due when you sell`
      : `in today's money`;

    if (outlook.reachYear !== null && outlook.reachYear < years) {
      headline.textContent =
        `You reach ${money(outlook.target)} in year ${outlook.reachYear} of ${years} ` +
        `— with ${years - outlook.reachYear} years still to run.`;
      detail.textContent =
        `On a typical run you would finish with ${money(outlook.endReal.p50)}, ${frame}. ` +
        `That is the middle outcome: about ${odds} in 100 futures get you there, ` +
        `and in the unluckiest you finish nearer ${money(outlook.endReal.p10)}.`;
    } else if (outlook.healthy) {
      headline.textContent =
        `You get to ${money(outlook.target)} — but only just, in year ${years}.`;
      detail.textContent =
        `On a typical run you finish with ${money(outlook.endReal.p50)}, ${frame}. ` +
        `About ${odds} in 100 futures get you there, so this plan has very ` +
        `little room in it.`;
    } else {
      headline.textContent =
        `You typically finish with ${money(outlook.endReal.p50)}, not ` +
        `${money(outlook.target)}.`;
      detail.textContent =
        `That is ${frame}, and it is the middle outcome — about ${odds} in 100 ` +
        `futures reach the goal. The three ways to close the gap are below, and ` +
        `every one of them is a real cost.`;
    }

    // The assumptions line names the period the growth came from, because a
    // number the reader inherited is a number they never chose (sol-028).
    $('sipAnsAssumptions')!.textContent =
      `Assuming ${inputs.expectedReturn}% growth with ${inputs.annualVolatility}% ` +
      `swings, ${inputs.expectedInflation}% inflation, and ` +
      `${Math.round(inputs.eqPct * 100)}% of it in shares.`;
  }

  function renderRemedies(inputs: any, remedies: any[]) {
    const box = $('sipAnsRemedies')!;
    const grid = $('sipAnsRemedyGrid')!;
    grid.innerHTML = '';

    if (!remedies.length) {
      box.classList.add('hidden');
      return;
    }
    box.classList.remove('hidden');

    for (const r of remedies) {
      if (r.outOfReach) continue;
      let title = '', sub = '', apply: () => void = () => {};

      if (r.kind === 'invest_more') {
        // The old page's REVERSE: GOAL-SEEK mode, in the reader's words.
        title = `Put away ₹${grp(r.delta)} more`;
        sub = `₹${grp(r.value)} a month instead`;
        apply = () => { ($('sipAnsMonthly') as HTMLInputElement).value = grp(r.value); };
      } else if (r.kind === 'wait_longer') {
        title = `Give it ${r.delta} more ${r.delta === 1 ? 'year' : 'years'}`;
        sub = `${r.value} years instead of ${inputs.horizonYears}`;
        apply = () => { ($('sipAnsYears') as HTMLInputElement).value = String(r.value); };
      } else {
        title = `Aim for ${money(r.value)} instead`;
        sub = `${money(r.delta)} less than you asked for`;
        apply = () => { ($('sipAnsTarget') as HTMLInputElement).value = grp(r.value); };
      }

      const odds = Math.round(r.odds * 100);
      const btn = document.createElement('button');
      btn.type = 'button';
      btn.className =
        'text-left rounded-xl border border-navy-200 dark:border-navy-700 bg-white/60 dark:bg-navy-900/40 ' +
        'p-4 hover:border-gold-500 dark:hover:border-gold-500 transition-colors ' +
        'focus:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-gold-500/50';
      // Both halves, always. "Typically" is a 50/50 word and the honest reading
      // of it is that the plan still misses in the other half - dressing that
      // up as safety is exactly the reduction dd-001 forbids.
      btn.innerHTML =
        `<span class="block text-sm font-semibold text-navy-900 dark:text-navy-100">${title}</span>` +
        `<span class="block text-xs text-navy-500 dark:text-navy-400 mt-1">${sub}</span>` +
        `<span class="block text-xs font-medium text-emerald-700 dark:text-emerald-400 mt-2">` +
        `${odds} out of 100 futures get there</span>` +
        `<span class="block text-xs text-navy-500 dark:text-navy-400 mt-0.5">` +
        `${100 - odds} still fall short</span>`;
      btn.addEventListener('click', () => { apply(); recalc(); });
      grid.appendChild(btn);
    }
  }

  function recalc() {
    // Entry edits land in the canonical fields before anything is read, so
    // there is only ever one place the numbers come from.
    syncAdvancedFromEntry();
    const inputs = readInputs();
    if (!inputs.monthlySip && !inputs.seedCapital) return;
    if (!inputs.targetRealWealth) return;

    // The three entry fields are a projection of the form below, not a second
    // copy of it. Pushing the canonical values back up keeps them identical
    // whichever end the reader typed at.
    syncEntryFromAdvanced();

    $('sipAnsHeadline')!.textContent = 'Working it out…';
    $('sipAnsDetail')!.textContent = '';

    worker?.postMessage(inputs);
  }

  function init() {
    worker = new Worker(new URL('../../workers/sipAdviceWorker.ts', import.meta.url), {
      type: 'module',
    });
    worker.onmessage = (e) => {
      if (!e.data?.ok) {
        $('sipAnsHeadline')!.textContent = 'Something went wrong working that out.';
        $('sipAnsDetail')!.textContent = 'Try changing one of the numbers above.';
        return;
      }
      const inputs = readInputs();

      // The levers and the growth track arrive after the answer, so neither
      // holds up the headline.
      if (e.data.stage === 'remedies') {
        renderRemedies(inputs, e.data.remedies);
        return;
      }
      if (e.data.stage === 'curve') {
        window.dispatchEvent(new CustomEvent('sip:curve', {
          detail: { inputs, curve: e.data.curve },
        }));
        return;
      }
      if (e.data.stage === 'sequence') {
        window.dispatchEvent(new CustomEvent('sip:sequence', {
          detail: { inputs, sequence: e.data.sequence },
        }));
        return;
      }
      if (e.data.stage === 'protection') {
        window.dispatchEvent(new CustomEvent('sip:protection', {
          detail: { inputs, protection: e.data.protection },
        }));
        return;
      }

      renderEscalation(inputs);
      renderAnswer(inputs, e.data.outlook);
      // Every surface subscribes to this rather than running its own
      // simulation - including the expert panel below, which used to own a
      // second worker and its own input reader (sol-026). `simulation` is the
      // raw engine result; it is what the panel renders.
      window.dispatchEvent(new CustomEvent('sip:result', {
        detail: { inputs, outlook: e.data.outlook, simulation: e.data.simulation },
      }));
    };

    // The compute host. Nothing else on the page runs anything; it asks, and
    // this answers - which is what makes disagreement impossible rather than
    // merely unlikely.
    window.addEventListener('sip:recompute', () => recalc());

    let t: any;
    for (const id of ['sipAnsMonthly', 'sipAnsYears', 'sipAnsTarget']) {
      $(id)?.addEventListener('input', () => {
        clearTimeout(t);
        t = setTimeout(recalc, 400);
      });
    }

    // Opens the last rung's first door - the controls - which is what a reader
    // clicking "change the assumptions" is asking for.
    // dd-017: a real-terms instalment quietly commits the reader to a much
    // larger cash figure later, and they are entitled to see it before they
    // agree to it. This is the affordability check, not a flourish.
    // Points at the control that actually exists, in the expert rung's
    // assumptions. A link that scrolls somewhere with nothing to change is a
    // promise the page does not keep. Giving rung 2 its own compact chooser is
    // on the gate - it is the rung about inflation eating money, so it is the
    // right home once it is built properly rather than bolted on now.
    $('sipAnsOpenContribution')?.addEventListener('click', () => {
      const rung = document.getElementById('rungSipExpert');
      if (!rung) return;
      const first = rung.querySelector('details') as HTMLDetailsElement | null;
      if (first) first.open = true;
      document.getElementById('sipContributionMode')?.scrollIntoView({
        behavior: 'smooth', block: 'center',
      });
    });

    $('sipAnsOpenDetail')?.addEventListener('click', () => {
      const rung = document.getElementById('rungSipExpert');
      if (!rung) return;
      const first = rung.querySelector('details') as HTMLDetailsElement | null;
      if (first) first.open = true;
      rung.scrollIntoView({ behavior: 'smooth', block: 'start' });
    });

    recalc();
  }

  if (document.readyState === 'loading') {
    document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', init);
  } else {
    init();
  }
</script>
